sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Haupaix et al. (2018), Inaba et al. (2019) & Lin et al. (2013) somite-prepatterned Agouti signaling, melanocyte gap-junction reaction-diffusion and feather-follicle ring-niche chevrons in galliform plumage stripes — MorphoEval overall 80.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 closes the single v2 remediation item with a reduced but machine-checked follicle-niche model and, for the first time in this loop, validates the script against numbers that Haupaix et al. (2018) actually publish: the wild-type / recessive-black / Fawn yellow-feather-row counts (4 / 2 / 5-6; simulated 4 / 2 / 6) and the qualitative centre-vs-edge yellow band gradient, with Fawn centre rows fully pheomelanic as the paper describes. Doing so exposed that the Pass 1-2 audits had credited two non-existent citations (a fabricated Haupaix title; a non-existent Inaba Science article) and a set of unsourced mm \"reference\" widths and \"bead\" experiments that the model was fitted to; these are now corrected or flagged in the vendored dataset. The overall score therefore falls from 92.2 to 80.9 even though the model grew: the remaining structure is honest but its oldest layer is still calibrated to numbers of unknown provenance. Overall 80.9/100 (faithfulness 78.6, reproducibility 86.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 469bf3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 78, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 80, Source and data traceability 82, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/avian_plumage_somite_stripes_comparison.png: rendered output of 2018-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes.py at 469bf3c, image/png, 1249752 B, 2393×1940 px, artifact_sha256 80cf4ed6c9ceafcaa92a29b89a4f12179acf9de9f1be8e80b058a57fc6b4e9a0 (sha256 80cf4ed6c9ceafcaa92a29b89a4f12179acf9de9f1be8e80b058a57fc6b4e9a0), spec_fingerprint b82c12bbaf2b8db3609a6e2056ad2f89a6a554142d599d056ea75d733384a4d7. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b82c12bbaf2b8db3609a6e2056ad2f89a6a554142d599d056ea75d733384a4d7; artifact_sha256: 80cf4ed6c9ceafcaa92a29b89a4f12179acf9de9f1be8e80b058a57fc6b4e9a0; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/avian_plumage_somite_stripes/avian_plumage_somite_stripes_reference.json=4cbeeca03b0939bf..., datasets/avian_plumage_somite_stripes/galliform_chick_stripes_specimen.jpg=78337aba30f62614..., datasets/avian_plumage_somite_stripes/scout_manifest.json=acb7ac44b807e24b...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-avian-plumage-somite-stripes-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Haupaix et al. (2018): galliform dorsal stripes form in two steps — the somite autonomously sets the position of dermal agouti expression bands (A1', A1, A2; quail somite -> pheasant host grafts, neural-tube grafts as control), and agouti dose then sets stripe width by controlling the duration of a transient yellow-production pulse within each feather; wild-type quail ly stripe = feather rows 2-5, recessive-black (agouti loss) rows 3-4, Fawn (agouti duplication) rows 1/2-6 with no eumelanin before hatching; yellow band longer at stripe centre than edge; stripe boundaries 2-4 mm (cb) and 3-9 mm (ly) from the midline at wing level | Inaba et al. (2019): quail melanocytes form periodic stripes cell-autonomously; connexin40 gap junctions tune the pattern (dominant-negative cx40 expands black, overexpression expands yellow); melanocytes instruct dermal ASIP expression | Lin et al. (2013): feather melanocyte progenitors form a horizontal ring niche in the proximal follicle and send melanocytes vertically into barb ridges; bars in Barred Plymouth Rock feathers are chevron-shaped when the follicle cylinder is opened from the posterior side and travel toward the anterior; pulp ASIP inhibits melanocyte differentiation (ASIP beads whiten feathers); reconstructed_in_script: A 2D somite-derived Gaussian agouti prepattern S_somite(y) coupled by relaxation beta_A (S - u) to a two-species activator-inhibitor PDE with cubic-saturating linearised kinetics and d = Dv/Du = 20; MC1R threshold switch u >= theta_A; AP orientation index and Ashman bimodality; negative controls beta_A = 0 and d = 1 | Pass 3: a 9-row-per-period hexagonal follicle lattice whose ring niches sample u(x_i, y_i); feather type [A_i >= theta] + [A_i - 2a >= theta] and yellow-pulse duty (1/pi) arccos((theta - (A_i - a))/a); an agouti dose series (x0.60 / x1.00 / x2.80) reproducing 2 / 4 / 6 yellow rows; each follicle rendered as a 3D cylinder and opened into the (ell, s) sheet with chevron band edges s_0 + k|ell|, swept over k and regressed back (max |k_meas - k| = 7e-4); Lean Theorems 4-5 | Pass 1-2 carry-overs: an analytic Gaussian-threshold species width w_y = 2 (1.13 sigma) sqrt(2 ln(A_0/theta)) for five species, a linear donor-autonomy chimera law alpha = 0.94, a fitted exponential dose-response for the 'bead' axis, and DoG segmentation of a CC BY-SA Coturnix japonica photograph (N = 4 stripes, yellow fraction 0.442); transfer_boundary: The mm calibration (Lambda = 0.95 mm, w_y = 0.42 mm, the 5-species widths) and the 'bead' regime widths were introduced in Pass 1 without a source; Haupaix et al. report stripe widths in feather rows and boundaries in mm from the midline, so the row-count validation (Pass 3) is the only width comparison against published values | The follicle model is a geometric + threshold reduction of Lin et al.: the chevron arises from a pigment switch propagating around the ring at rate omega while cells rise at v_z (k = v_z/(r_f omega)); no barb-ridge helical displacement, pulp ASIP diffusion, progenitor-depletion feedback or regeneration cycle is solved; a, k and the dose multipliers are fitted, not measured | The reverse chimeras (pheasant -> quail, guineafowl -> quail) are extrapolations of the quail -> pheasant result; the PDE integrates a cubic linearisation, not the rational Gierer-Meinhardt kinetics written in the reference JSON; does_not_claim: Quantitative reproduction of Haupaix Fig. 3C / fig. S6 relative yellow band lengths or of the midline-distance boundaries, a mechanistic derivation of the agouti fold-change in RB/Fa strains, the melanocyte cell-autonomy or cx40 experiments of Inaba et al., the Barred Plymouth Rock progenitor-depletion mechanism of Lin et al., or a side-by-side comparison with the papers' own figures (none are vendored)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2018-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes.py:1410 — `--species` is parsed but never used. Wire it to the species panel / follicle readout (per-species rows_per_period and A_0) or remove it.",
            "remediation needed: 2018-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes.py:286-289 vs datasets/avian_plumage_somite_stripes/avian_plumage_somite_stripes_reference.json governing_pde — the solver integrates a cubic-saturating linearisation around (0.46, 0.46) while the docstring and JSON write rational Gierer-Meinhardt kinetics alpha_u u^2 / (v (1 + kappa u^2)). Either integrate the rational form (and re-derive the Lean Theorem 3 Jacobian from its fixed point) or rewrite the JSON/docstring to the cubic model.",
            "remediation needed: 2018-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes.py:339-361 and 452-488 — species yellow widths come from an analytic Gaussian-threshold formula with an unexplained sigma_eff = 1.13 sigma, and the dose axis from a fitted exponential delta_w = 0.48 (1 - exp(-0.82 dose)); the PDE's own quail yellow fraction is 0.35, not the 0.448 reported. Derive species and dose widths from the PDE + lattice (as the Pass 3 mutant panel already does) and drop the formulas.",
            "remediation needed: 2018-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes.py:395-449 — the pheasant -> quail and guineafowl -> quail chimeras and alpha_donor = 0.94 are extrapolations; Haupaix et al. report quail somites -> pheasant hosts (and neural-tube controls). Keep the reported direction as validation, label the others as predictions, and add the neural-tube negative control.",
            "remediation needed: 2018-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes.py:534-542 and 659-724 — niche dip a = 0.20, chevron pitch k = 0.35 and the RB/Fa dose multipliers 0.60 / 2.80 are fitted to the target row counts and Fawn saturates (any scale >= 2.5 gives 6 rows). Calibrate a against digitised relative yellow band lengths and k against Lin (2013) fig. S9 chevron angles; add barb-ridge helical displacement so k is derived from (v_z, r_f, omega) rather than set.",
            "remediation needed: 2018-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes.py:574-656 — the lattice y-feather fraction (0.444, 9-row quantisation) differs from the body pigment-map fraction (0.35, 80-row grid) by 0.094. Resolve by sampling the lattice on a finer grid or by reporting the body fraction in feather-row units, and tighten self-test check 10 from 0.12 to < 0.03.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/avian_plumage_somite_stripes/avian_plumage_somite_stripes_reference.json galliform_species_panel and agouti_bead_perturbation_regimes — mm widths, Lambda = 0.95 mm and the five 'bead' regimes have no published source (now flagged in pass3_provenance_flags). Replace them with the paper's own data: midline distances (cb 2-4 mm, ly 3-9 mm at wing level), feather-row counts, and digitised Fig. 3C / fig. S6 relative yellow band lengths; re-pin.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/avian_plumage_somite_stripes/scout_manifest.json — not re-audited in Pass 3; check it for the old Haupaix/Inaba citations and vendor PMIDs for Lin (2013) and Bailleul (2019); vendor or digitise one paper figure (Haupaix Fig. 1A flat skin or Lin fig. S9) so specimen-match can be judged side by side.",
            "remediation needed: morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_010_avian_plumage_somite_stripes.lean:132-157 — Theorem 4 treats k as a free integer; add the definitional link k = v_z / (r_f omega) (scaled integers) and prove the bar limit as omega -> large; Theorem 5 proves the trichotomy but not the duty formula's monotonicity, which needs reals (Mathlib) and is carried as out of reach in core Lean." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.809"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Slot 010 Pass 3 autonomous loop assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

